<div class="page-head">
  <h1 class="section-title"><span class="gradient-text">JEV</span> — decision sidecar</h1>
  <p>An optional second opinion from TypeSafe's System One model. After a proof, the runner projects the manifest into a compact state object and asks four narrow questions. The answers fold into a verdict — and that verdict never overrides the deterministic gates or picks a candidate.</p>
</div>

<div class="grid-2" style="align-items:stretch;">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>failure_mode <span class="tech-tag">choice</span></h3>
    <p style="color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:0.75rem;">
      Which failure signature best describes this candidate — judged only from the
      preflight measurements and finding details.
    </p>
    <div style="margin-top:0.75rem;">
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">screen_explosion</div>
        <div class="a">Far more distinct colours or screens than the contract allows.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">continuous_tone</div>
        <div class="a">A smooth tonal ramp was traced, which flat-colour printing cannot reproduce.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">geometry_overload</div>
        <div class="a">Paths carry far more nodes than the limit — slow to RIP, hard to hand-edit.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">palette_mismatch</div>
        <div class="a">Declared colours fall outside the contract palette.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">render_or_tool_failure</div>
        <div class="a">The proof or PDF could not be produced, or a tool was missing.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">no_hard_failure</div>
        <div class="a">No hard finding is present in the supplied measurements.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">unclear</div>
        <div class="a">The measurements don't identify one clear failure signature.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>print_route <span class="tech-tag">choice</span></h3>
    <p style="color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:0.75rem;">
      Which production route fits this artwork as measured.
    </p>
    <div style="margin-top:0.75rem;">
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">screen_spot_low</div>
        <div class="a">Spot-colour screen printing within the contract colour budget.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">screen_spot_multi</div>
        <div class="a">Spot-colour screen printing — but above budget; more screens or a redesign.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">process_halftone</div>
        <div class="a">Four-colour / simulated process required because tone must survive.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">dtg_or_dtf</div>
        <div class="a">Direct-to-garment or direct-to-film fits better than screen printing.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">unsuitable</div>
        <div class="a">No route reproduces this artwork as measured without rework.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">unclear</div>
        <div class="a">The measurements don't determine a production route.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>tonal_structure <span class="tech-tag">score</span></h3>
    <p style="color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:0.75rem;">
      How faithfully the trace preserved the source's tonal structure — judged only
      from measured colour count, ramp and coverage numbers.
    </p>
    <div class="jev-grid" style="margin-top:0.75rem;">
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">Broken</div>
        <div class="a">Tone collapsed into noise or non-printing blends.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">Flat</div>
        <div class="a">Tonal range reduced to a few hard steps with visible banding.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">Retained</div>
        <div class="a">A coherent tonal read survives in flat colours.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">Engraving-grade</div>
        <div class="a">Dense, ordered tonal structure — deliberate screen/engraving look.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;">evidence_is_actionable <span class="tech-tag">noul</span></h3>
    <p style="color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:0.75rem;">
      Do the supplied measurements contain enough reliable evidence to act on a
      production decision, given their stated limitations?
    </p>
    <div class="jev-grid" style="margin-top:0.75rem;">
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">true</div>
        <div class="a">Source, render and PDF evidence present; limitations don't block a decision.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">false</div>
        <div class="a">A required measurement is missing, failed, or is an estimate whose limitation blocks the decision.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>The verdict</h3>
    <p style="color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:0.9rem;margin-top:0.75rem;">
      Typed answers fold into a thresholded verdict. Run by hand, the annotator
      writes it as a <span class="mono"><stem>.jev.json</span> sidecar next to the
      manifest; run through this runner it comes back in the response body
      instead, because the job directory is not the runner's to write in. Do not
      go looking for the sidecar file on a runner job — it is never created.
      Any answer whose certainty falls below the floor is surfaced in
      <span class="mono">low_confidence</span> instead of being reported as settled fact.
    </p>
    <div class="log-console" style="margin-top:0.75rem;max-height:280px;">
<pre>{
  "headline": "screen_explosion",
  "print_route": "process_halftone",
  "tonal_score": 0.95,
  "tonal_label": "Flat",
  "evidence_actionable": false,
  "low_confidence": ["tonal_structure"],
  "confidence_floor": 0.6
}</pre>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Confidence rules</h3>
    <div style="margin-top:0.75rem;">
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">choice <span class="tech-tag">confidence 0..1</span></div>
        <div class="a">Real field — used directly.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">score <span class="tech-tag">probabilities</span></div>
        <div class="a">Reported <span class="mono">confidence</span> is always 0.0 — the annotator reads <span class="mono">max(probabilities)</span> instead.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="jev-card">
        <div class="q">noul <span class="tech-tag">value = P(true)</span></div>
        <div class="a">No separate confidence — certainty is <span class="mono">2·|noul − 0.5|</span>.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<p style="color:var(--text-tertiary);font-size:0.8rem;margin-top:1rem;">
  Jev is advisory only. The deterministic gates in the pipeline remain the source of truth;
  it never ranks candidates and never picks a winner. On a proof page, the
  <strong style="color:var(--text-secondary)">Ask Jev</strong> button triggers the run through the runner.
</p>
